<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh port strike ends.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh port strike ends.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Normal activities resumed at Bangladesh's main Chittagong port on Wednesday night after employees ended a day-long strike, port officials said.</p>
<p>They said strikers returned to work after the authorities said they would consider their demands for higher wages and benefits.</p>
<p>The strike disrupted cargo handling and ship movement for about 10 hours, officials said.</p>
<p>The port workers union, however, gave the authorities a 10-day ultimatum to accept their demands, they said.</p>
<p>Some 28 ships were awaiting berth at the port on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, dock workers at the country's second port at Mongla warned on Wednesday that they would go for an indefinite strike unless authorities met their demand for higher wages before November 27, port officials said.</p>
</text>
